# said -- words said another way aloud, for voice (the EBaC integration's
# answers): a word a voice can't read as it is written, such as a name
# with no vowels, which it guesses at ("יהוה" was said as "yo"). See
# "Voice" in readme.architecture.
#
# One word to a line: the word as the text has it, "=", then what to say.
# Only whole words are changed, not one inside a longer word. A word with
# vowel points, or with a letter joined to its front, is another word, and
# needs a line of its own.
#
# Only for what is spoken: the screen, the text in voice answers, and
# searching all keep the word as the text has it.

יהוה = Adonai
